# Installed by the base metapackage as /usr/lib/modprobe.d/@DISTRO_ID@-thunderbolt.conf; mkinitramfs
# copies it into the initramfs, where the thunderbolt driver loads.
#
# When the driver sets up a DisplayPort tunnel to a Thunderbolt display, it waits for the DPRX
# capability read, which only the GPU driver (i915 here) can complete, and by default gives up
# after 12 s (TB_DPRX_TIMEOUT in drivers/thunderbolt/tunnel.c), tears the tunnel down and does not
# retry. i915 loads from the root filesystem, after the disk encryption passphrase, so a
# passphrase typed 12 s or more after the driver started left the display dark until it was
# replugged (Apple Studio Display on the Legion laptop, 2026-10-15). -1 waits until the GPU
# driver answers; the wait runs as delayed work and holds nothing else up.
options thunderbolt dprx_timeout=-1
